{"kind":"assert","text":"Addition to the identifiers build (05d618e2, ruling c0a795e7): the\nfold refuses a redundant spelling from the cutover.\n\nHead F (K-spell, 2ad35350) adds the canonical-spelling mode to\n`validateDefinition` and turns it on only where a definition is\nauthored (ruling on 718769a3). It leaves every fold call site at\nthe default, because old-format rooms hold recorded definitions in\nthe redundant spelling.\n\nThe identifiers cutover retires those rooms. In the build under\n05d618e2, every call site that admits a definition into a\nnew-format room passes `canonical: true`: scope creation,\napplication install, the rules scope, the directory and the\narchive reads. Replay of a new-format journal uses the same mode.\nThe recorded demo release in the old spelling is not installable\nafter the cutover. The planner signs a new release from the\ncanonical sources before the rooms are recreated.\n\nThis item needs F on main. It adds no separate head. It belongs to\nthe head that changes the admission paths.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}